  "facts": {
    "1858": "Hyde Park ground, Sheffield, 1858: All-England Eleven v 22 of Hallam; H. H. Stephenson took three wickets in three balls; a collection was taken and a hat bought for him (popular account; a 2024 ADS-L post finds a July 1858 'claiming a new hat' report, so the custom may be slightly older)",
    "print": "'hat trick' in print by 1865",
