  },
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Why are three goals in a game called a hat-trick?",
      "scene": {
        "bg": "blue",
        "hook": true,
        "type": "tally",
        "steps": [
          {
            "type": "tally",
            "n": 3,
            "cols": 3,
            "icon": "ball",
            "labels": [
              "GOAL 1",
              "GOAL 2",
              "GOAL 3"
            ],
            "count": true,
            "w": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "statement",
            "text": "HAT|TRICK?",
            "hi": 0,
            "size": 165,
            "w": 9
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Well, the hat was real. And it was won in cricket, not football.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "picture",
        "steps": [
          {
            "type": "picture",
            "image": "top_hat",
            "big": "THE HAT WAS REAL",
            "bigSize": 120,
            "bigY": 1300,
            "w": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "picture",
            "image": "hattrick1858",
            "label": "CRICKET",
            "w": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Sheffield, 1858. The All-England Eleven took on twenty-two players from Hallam.",
      "scene": {
        "bg": "blue",
        "type": "years",
        "steps": [
          {
            "type": "years",
            "items": [
              {
                "year": "1858",
                "top": "SHEFFIELD",
                "label": "Hyde Park ground",
                "head": "#1d3fa0"
              }
            ],
            "w": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "picture",
            "image": "hattrick1858",
            "label": "ALL-ENGLAND XI v HALLAM",
            "w": 3
          },
          {
            "type": "statement",
            "text": "11 v 22",
            "size": 300,
            "w": 7
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Then their bowler, H. H. Stephenson, took three wickets with three balls in a row.",
      "scene": {
        "bg": "green",
        "type": "picture",
        "steps": [
          {
            "type": "picture",
            "image": "stephenson_bowl",
            "label": "H. H. STEPHENSON",
            "w": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "tally",
            "n": 3,
            "cols": 3,
            "mark": "OUT",
            "markCol": "#e2384a",
            "labels": [
              "BALL 1",
              "BALL 2",
              "BALL 3"
            ],
            "title": "3 BALLS, 3 WICKETS",
            "w": 7
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Almost unheard of. So the crowd passed round a collection, and bought him a brand new hat.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "statement",
        "steps": [
          {
            "type": "statement",
            "text": "ALMOST|UNHEARD OF",
            "hi": 1,
            "size": 165,
            "w": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "picture",
            "image": "hat_collection",
            "label": "A COLLECTION",
            "w": 5
          },
          {
            "type": "picture",
            "image": "hat_presented",
            "big": "A NEW HAT",
            "bigSize": 170,
            "bigY": 1350,
            "w": 11
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Three wickets in three balls became a 'hat-trick'. By 1865, the word was in print.",
      "scene": {
        "bg": "purple",
        "type": "statement",
        "steps": [
          {
            "type": "statement",
            "text": "3 IN 3 =|HAT-TRICK",
            "hi": 1,
            "size": 165,
            "w": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "years",
            "items": [
              {
                "year": "1858",
                "top": "THE HAT",
                "label": "Sheffield"
              },
              {
                "year": "1865",
                "top": "IN PRINT",
                "label": "'Hat trick'",
                "head": "#1ea85a"
              }
            ],
            "w": 8
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Football borrowed it. Now it means three goals in one game.",
      "scene": {
        "bg": "blue",
        "type": "picture",
        "steps": [
          {
            "type": "picture",
            "image": "hat_presented",
            "big": "FOOTBALL BORROWED IT",
            "bigSize": 110,
            "bigY": 1350,
            "w": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "tally",
            "n": 3,
            "cols": 3,
            "icon": "ball",
            "labels": [
              "GOAL 1",
              "GOAL 2",
              "GOAL 3"
            ],
            "title": "ONE GAME",
            "w": 6
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The rarest kind? A perfect hat-trick: left foot, right foot, and a header.",
      "scene": {
        "bg": "orange",
        "type": "statement",
        "steps": [
          {
            "type": "statement",
            "text": "THE PERFECT|HAT-TRICK",
            "hi": 1,
            "size": 165,
            "w": 0
          },
          {
            "type": "statement",
            "text": "LEFT FOOT",
            "size": 190,
            "w": 6
          },
          {
            "type": "statement",
            "text": "LEFT FOOT|RIGHT FOOT",
            "size": 165,
            "w": 8
          },
          {
            "type": "statement",
            "text": "LEFT FOOT|RIGHT FOOT|HEADER",
            "hi": 2,
            "size": 135,
            "w": 12
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The fastest in Premier League history? Sadio Mané. Two minutes fifty-six seconds, for Southampton against Aston Villa.",
      "scene": {
        "bg": "red",
        "type": "statement",
        "steps": [
          {
            "type": "statement",
            "text": "FASTEST|IN THE PL?",
            "hi": 1,
            "size": 165,
            "w": 0
          },
          {
